{"items":[{"tags":["python","string"],"owner":{"account_id":5755,"reputation":40949,"user_id":9435,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":78,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/4hJxhPtL.png?s=256","display_name":"oneself","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/9435/oneself"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":1757489,"protected_date":1365668977,"accepted_answer_id":931095,"answer_count":14,"score":1714,"last_activity_date":1703315488,"creation_date":1243735810,"last_edit_date":1703315488,"question_id":931092,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/931092/how-do-i-reverse-a-string-in-python","title":"How do I reverse a string in Python?","body":"<p>There is no built in <code>reverse</code> method for Python's <code>str</code> object. How can I reverse a string?</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","parsing","floating-point","type-conversion","integer"],"owner":{"account_id":14717,"reputation":70476,"user_id":30529,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":94,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/f3a3491c1c83e8c62151752162184627?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Tristan Havelick","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/30529/tristan-havelick"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":4896576,"protected_date":1365593283,"accepted_answer_id":379910,"answer_count":34,"score":2786,"last_activity_date":1780069833,"creation_date":1229651546,"last_edit_date":1700761208,"question_id":379906,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/379906/how-do-i-parse-a-string-to-a-float-or-int","title":"How do I parse a string to a float or int?","body":"<p>How can I convert an <code>str</code> to a <code>float</code>?</p>\n<pre><code>&quot;545.2222&quot; -&gt; 545.2222\n</code></pre>\n<p>Or an <code>str</code> to a <code>int</code>?</p>\n<pre><code>&quot;31&quot; -&gt; 31\n</code></pre>\n<hr />\n<p><sub>For the reverse, see <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/961632\">Convert integer to string in Python</a> and <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/1317558\">Converting a float to a string without rounding it</a>.</sub></p>\n<p><sub>Please instead use <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/20449427\">How can I read inputs as numbers?</a> to close duplicate questions where OP received a string <em>from user input</em> and immediately wants to convert it, or was hoping for <code>input</code> (in 3.x) to convert the type automatically.</sub></p>\n"},{"tags":["python"],"owner":{"account_id":15266657,"reputation":37,"user_id":11015083,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-nD2N-k6cufw/AAAAAAAAAAI/AAAAAAAAABg/5JjaFfaWz0I/s256-rj/photo.jpg","display_name":"Robert Hitch","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/11015083/robert-hitch"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":326,"accepted_answer_id":54624064,"answer_count":3,"score":-2,"last_activity_date":1597926718,"creation_date":1549859981,"question_id":54624050,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/54624050/defining-a-function-to-reverse-a-string-in-python","title":"Defining a function to reverse a string in Python","body":"<p>I wrote this function to reverse a string in Python but it doesn't work, I just get the output: \"gnirts tupni\"</p>\n\n<p>Any idea where I'm going wrong? </p>\n\n<pre><code>def transcribe_1(input_string):\n output_string = 'input string'[::-1]\n return output_string\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n  print(transcribe_1('Reverse this string'))\n</code></pre>\n"},{"tags":["python","string","performance"],"owner":{"account_id":3106782,"reputation":386,"user_id":2629402,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":45,"profile_image":"https://graph.facebook.com/777104332/picture?type=large","display_name":"Ashmeet Singh","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/2629402/ashmeet-singh"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":21906,"answer_count":2,"score":5,"last_activity_date":1687816504,"creation_date":1461978739,"last_edit_date":1687816504,"question_id":36949665,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/36949665/fastest-way-to-reverse-a-string-in-python","title":"Fastest way to reverse a string in python","body":"<p>I was able to come up with two different ways to reverse a string in Python.</p>\n<p>Common sense dictates that code with more lines should run slower. I reversed a the string in two ways.</p>\n<p>Implementation 1:</p>\n<pre><code>&quot;&quot;.join(reversed(map(lambda x:x,st)))\n</code></pre>\n<p>Implementation 2:</p>\n<pre><code>st[::-1]\n</code></pre>\n<p>These have similar performance. Even for a 20000-character string, the difference is less than one millisecond.</p>\n<p>I think the first one should be a slower approach because it performs 3x more operations.</p>\n<p>Why am I not seeing a performance difference?</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","list","reverse"],"owner":{"account_id":399807,"reputation":3961,"user_id":765409,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":90,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/9e387ebc6f0bab782739d2a53b425c2a?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Louis93","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/765409/louis93"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":9682,"closed_date":1309652111,"accepted_answer_id":6557984,"answer_count":3,"score":3,"last_activity_date":1309622786,"creation_date":1309621451,"last_edit_date":1495542331,"question_id":6557950,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/6557950/python-reverse-a-string","closed_reason":"exact duplicate","title":"Python: reverse a string","body":"<blockquote>\n  <p><strong>Possible Duplicate:</strong><br>\n  <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/931092/reverse-a-string-in-python\">Reverse a string in Python</a>  </p>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n\n<p>I understand that data in Python (strings) are stored like lists</p>\n\n<p>Example:</p>\n\n<pre><code>string1 = \"foo\"\n\"foo\"[1] = \"o\"\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>How would I use the list.reverse function to reverse the characters in a string? Such that I input \"foo\" and get returned back \"oof\"</p>\n"},{"tags":["python"],"owner":{"account_id":30031921,"reputation":1,"user_id":23014819,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJ-OG7CuGdN6VM_mDlGU02Y8BO4YsHOXzcAq-54_81E0yg=k-s256","display_name":"Walter","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/23014819/walter"},"is_answered":false,"view_count":118,"closed_date":1701494074,"answer_count":2,"score":-7,"last_activity_date":1701494086,"creation_date":1701492469,"question_id":77589182,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/77589182/how-to-reverse-a-string-in-python-and-the-reversal-should-contain-the-reversal-c","closed_reason":"Duplicate","title":"How to reverse a string in python and the reversal should contain the reversal case letters","body":"<p><strong>Question:</strong>\nI'm new to Python and trying to reverse a string. What's the simplest way to achieve this? I've seen a few methods online, but I'm not sure which one is the most straightforward and commonly used. Could someone provide a clear example of how to reverse a string in Python?</p>\n<p>i was trying to reverse a string like &quot;Hello world&quot; to get output &quot;DLROW OLLEh&quot;</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","python-3.x"],"owner":{"account_id":7502276,"reputation":21,"user_id":5700147,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/ed447f8ebc3c9340eb99a7da013e6272?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Invader","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/5700147/invader"},"is_answered":false,"view_count":120,"closed_date":1452004364,"answer_count":1,"score":-2,"last_activity_date":1452005068,"creation_date":1452003850,"last_edit_date":1452005068,"question_id":34613955,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/34613955/python-reverse-a-string","closed_reason":"Duplicate","title":"Python (reverse a string)","body":"<p>Hello everyone im trying to reverse a string in python but i cant get it to work. I tried using reversed but it didnt work. I found the replacment for it but it i cant get it to work properly. Explenanation and help would be appriciated.</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://i.sstatic.net/sb3Du.png\" rel=\"nofollow\">code</a></p>\n\n<pre><code>word=\"cba\"\nword[::1]\nprint (word)\n</code></pre>\n"},{"tags":["python","python-3.x","string","reverse"],"owner":{"account_id":16217955,"reputation":9,"user_id":11710278,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://lh6.googleusercontent.com/-_ZldC_Tt-M0/AAAAAAAAAAI/AAAAAAAAAAA/ACHi3rcj7oP73bBktKC1SfsORbHGp74anw/s256-rj/photo.jpg","display_name":"Robert L","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/11710278/robert-l"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":480,"answer_count":3,"score":0,"last_activity_date":1681033981,"creation_date":1561661367,"last_edit_date":1561663216,"question_id":56797120,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/56797120/how-exactly-is-this-code-working-to-reverse-a-string-in-python","title":"How exactly is this code working to reverse a string in Python","body":"<pre class=\"lang-py prettyprint-override\"><code>def reverse(x):\n    output = \"\"\n    for c in x:\n        output = c + output\n\n    return output\n\nprint(reverse(\"Hello\"))\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>This code works fine to reverse a string in Python, I just can't seem to understand why it is working and how.</p>\n\n<p>If, for example, I iterate through a string, usually it will iterate and print starting from \"H\" and work its way down to \"O.\" How is it that here, it's going backwards?</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","in-place"],"owner":{"account_id":16131791,"reputation":1,"user_id":11645243,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://graph.facebook.com/2122290127882959/picture?type=large","display_name":"Khizar Khan","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/11645243/khizar-khan"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":5746,"closed_date":1560467713,"answer_count":1,"score":-1,"last_activity_date":1560467600,"creation_date":1560467117,"question_id":56589536,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/56589536/reverse-the-string-in-place-in-python","closed_reason":"Duplicate","title":"Reverse the string (IN PLACE) in python","body":"<p>I want to know how to reverse a string in python without creating a new one. </p>\n\n<p>I can't seem to get it.</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","string"],"owner":{"account_id":10912952,"reputation":5,"user_id":8021713,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/2234d2c03a94b802eea37ec260319406?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Trogi","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/8021713/trogi"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":61,"closed_date":1494965438,"accepted_answer_id":44010535,"answer_count":1,"score":-5,"last_activity_date":1494965060,"creation_date":1494964630,"question_id":44010506,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/44010506/how-tomreverse-a-string-in-python","closed_reason":"Duplicate","title":"How tomreverse a string in python?","body":"<p>I have a string: </p>\n\n<pre><code>ahdeg\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>What is the best way to reverse a string in python so it would be: </p>\n\n<pre><code>gedha\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>Anything would help, thanks! </p>\n"},{"tags":["python","string","performance"],"owner":{"account_id":24223033,"reputation":31,"user_id":18177923,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/95c4fa3a12588b7e14974f89c7220620?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"FriedRobot","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/18177923/friedrobot"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":6807,"closed_date":1687762338,"answer_count":1,"score":-2,"last_activity_date":1687761960,"creation_date":1687759364,"question_id":76553893,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/76553893/what-is-the-most-efficient-way-to-reverse-a-string-in-python","closed_reason":"Duplicate","title":"What is the most efficient way to reverse a string in Python?","body":"<p>I'm looking for the most efficient method to reverse a string in Python. While there are several approaches to accomplish this task, I want to know which technique provides the best performance in terms of execution time.</p>\n<p>Here's an example of the straightforward approach I've been using:</p>\n<pre><code>def reverse_string(input_string):\nreturn input_string[::-1]\noriginal_string = &quot;Hello, World!&quot;\nreversed_string = reverse_string(original_string)\nprint(reversed_string)\n</code></pre>\n<p>However, I'm curious if there are other techniques or built-in functions that can achieve the same result but with better efficiency. I'm specifically interested in approaches that can handle strings of varying lengths, including very long strings.</p>\n"},{"tags":["python"],"owner":{"account_id":4901290,"reputation":27,"user_id":3949449,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/odVpP.jpg?s=256","display_name":"Gunwant Suryawanshi","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/3949449/gunwant-suryawanshi"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":761,"closed_date":1476713652,"accepted_answer_id":34743809,"answer_count":2,"score":-6,"last_activity_date":1453500930,"creation_date":1452601753,"last_edit_date":1452606508,"question_id":34743736,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/34743736/how-to-reverse-a-string-in-python","closed_reason":"Duplicate","title":"How to reverse a string in python","body":"<p>How to reverse string in python?  my input string is \"Hey Gun\" now i want to display \"Gun Hey\" as output.  I have tried using slice operator like [::-1] but it won't shows proper output how it works in python?</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","string","reverse"],"owner":{"account_id":17106385,"reputation":1,"user_id":12378325,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/77d891eeb5a048cdd1df550e8e5c1074?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"malikonakci","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/12378325/malikonakci"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":439,"closed_date":1676028974,"answer_count":1,"score":-1,"last_activity_date":1676027501,"creation_date":1676027330,"question_id":75410298,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/75410298/reversing-a-string-including-the-first-letter-in-python","closed_reason":"Duplicate","title":"Reversing a string including the first letter in python","body":"<p>I am trying to reverse a string in python but i cannot include the first letter.</p>\n<p>I tried this code:\na = &quot;Helloworld&quot;\nprint(a[3:0:-1])</p>\n<p>but it doesn't work.\nI also tried:\na = &quot;Helloworld&quot;\nprint(a[3:-1:-1])</p>\n<p>It displays nothing when i try this.</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","string","recursion"],"owner":{"account_id":710897,"reputation":1269,"user_id":615585,"user_type":"unregistered","accept_rate":91,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/15cc7d7366abc605b615390c6b42832d?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Eric","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/615585/eric"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":80582,"accepted_answer_id":5532914,"answer_count":8,"score":14,"last_activity_date":1655388004,"creation_date":1301868774,"last_edit_date":1616396177,"question_id":5532902,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/5532902/python-reversing-a-string-using-recursion","title":"Python reversing a string using recursion","body":"<p>I want to use recursion to reverse a string in python so it displays the characters backwards (i.e &quot;Hello&quot; will become &quot;olleh&quot;/&quot;o l l e h&quot;.</p>\n<p>I wrote one that does it iteratively:</p>\n<pre><code>def Reverse( s ):\n    result = &quot;&quot;\n    n = 0\n    start = 0\n    while ( s[n:] != &quot;&quot; ):\n        while ( s[n:] != &quot;&quot; and s[n] != ' ' ):\n            n = n + 1\n            result = s[ start: n ] + &quot; &quot; + result\n            start = n\n    return result\n</code></pre>\n<p>But how exactly do I do this recursively? I am confused on this part, especially because I don't work with python and recursion much.</p>\n<p>Any help would be appreciated.</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","string","recursion"],"owner":{"account_id":8212551,"reputation":29,"user_id":6180101,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/53b25d2130386bb75392aeee2a5d5993?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"nnizh13","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/6180101/nnizh13"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":359,"answer_count":4,"score":1,"last_activity_date":1597929658,"creation_date":1585450366,"last_edit_date":1585451066,"question_id":60909618,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/60909618/reversing-a-string-recursively-in-python","title":"Reversing a String recursively in Python","body":"<p>I am trying to reverse a string recursively in Python, however, this solution does not work</p>\n\n<pre><code>def reverseString(self, s):\n    \"\"\"\n    :type s: List[str]\n    :rtype: None Do not return anything, modify s in-place instead.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(s) == 0:\n        return s\n    s[0], s[-1] = s[-1], s[0]\n    self.reverseString(s[1:-1])\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>For the sample input [\"h\",\"e\",\"l\",\"l\",\"o\"], I get the output [\"o\",\"e\",\"l\",\"l\",\"h\"]. Can anyone exlpain why this does not work?</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","string"],"owner":{"account_id":12225501,"reputation":49,"user_id":8923263,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/d083b58de6ae5e86c1dc75e92e8035ca?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Idreams","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/8923263/idreams"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":2524,"answer_count":5,"score":3,"last_activity_date":1510396604,"creation_date":1510387015,"last_edit_date":1510396604,"question_id":47235740,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/47235740/reverse-a-string-in-python-but-keep-numbers-in-original-order","title":"Reverse a string in Python but keep numbers in original order","body":"<p>I can reverse a string using the <code>[::- 1]</code> syntax. Take note of the example below:</p>\n\n<pre><code>text_in = 'I am 25 years old'\nrev_text = text_in[::-1]\nprint rev_text\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>Output:</p>\n\n<pre><code>dlo sraey 52 ma I\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>How can I reverse only the letters while keeping the numbers in order?</p>\n\n<p>The desired result for the example is <code>'dlo sraey 25 ma I'</code>.</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","python-3.x","string","slice"],"owner":{"account_id":10662640,"reputation":1756,"user_id":7850174,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/5b2979928f9ef83358dce4682bc9cbf6?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"coderina","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/7850174/coderina"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":110,"answer_count":1,"score":0,"last_activity_date":1580838961,"creation_date":1560948078,"last_edit_date":1569230035,"question_id":56667906,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/56667906/is-reversing-string-in-python-in-place-method","title":"Is reversing string in python in-place method?","body":"<p>Following is the easiest way of reversing a string in python:</p>\n\n<pre><code>    string = 'SHWETA'\n    print(string[: : -1])\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>I just wanted to know if this code is executing in-place or taking any extra space.</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","python-2.7"],"owner":{"account_id":2625959,"reputation":63,"user_id":2272942,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7929a28f98d39e08140b7c04a1e3a778?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"user2272942","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/2272942/user2272942"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":748,"answer_count":3,"score":5,"last_activity_date":1365747861,"creation_date":1365744121,"last_edit_date":1365744301,"question_id":15963654,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/15963654/reversing-a-string-in-python-based-on-block-size-in-python","title":"Reversing a string in python based on block size in python","body":"<p>Im trying to reverse a string based on the block size given</p>\n\n<p>for example </p>\n\n<p><code>\"the price of food is 12 dollars\"</code> and im given a block size of 4 </p>\n\n<p>i want the end result to be: </p>\n\n<pre><code>food of price the dollars 12 is\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>im not sure how to input this into python any help would be appreciated \ni need this to work for any block size </p>\n"},{"tags":["python"],"owner":{"account_id":13849881,"reputation":293,"user_id":10578350,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/dda4d8e575b06b8975da648b005237e6?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Rishavv","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/10578350/rishavv"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":481,"closed_date":1558520267,"accepted_answer_id":56254522,"answer_count":1,"score":-1,"last_activity_date":1558520461,"creation_date":1558520057,"question_id":56254477,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/56254477/unable-to-get-the-reversed-string-in-python","closed_reason":"Duplicate","title":"Unable to get the reversed string in python","body":"<p>I am writing a program in python to reverse a string using function reversed but not getting the output .</p>\n\n<pre><code>myStr=\"hello\"\nrev=reversed(myStr)\nprint(rev)\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>I am getting the Output - reversed object at 0x000001823DF7DD68</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","string","function","loops","reverse"],"owner":{"account_id":9875177,"reputation":105,"user_id":7313219,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":40,"profile_image":"https://graph.facebook.com/10154285200903877/picture?type=large","display_name":"Daniel B","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/7313219/daniel-b"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":51722,"closed_date":1482770233,"accepted_answer_id":41322371,"answer_count":4,"score":3,"last_activity_date":1482709244,"creation_date":1482679156,"last_edit_date":1482709244,"question_id":41322315,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/41322315/reversing-a-string-in-python-using-a-loop","closed_reason":"Duplicate","title":"Reversing a string in Python using a loop?","body":"<p>I'm stuck at an exercise where I need to reverse a random string in a function using only a loop (for loop or while?).</p>\n\n<p>I can not use <code>\".join(reversed(string))</code> or <code>string[::-1]</code> methods here so it's a bit tricky.</p>\n\n<p>My code looks something like this:</p>\n\n<pre><code>def reverse(text):\n    while len(text) &gt; 0:\n        print text[(len(text)) - 1],\n        del(text[(len(text)) - 1]\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>I use the <code>,</code> to print out every single letter in text on the same line!</p>\n\n<p>I get invalid syntax on <code>del(text[(len(text)) - 1]</code></p>\n\n<p>Any suggestions?</p>\n"},{"tags":["python"],"owner":{"account_id":110788,"reputation":396,"user_id":293037,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/37af4ff058fb9f42cbfac6f51af44097?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Tomaž Pisanski","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/293037/toma%c5%be-pisanski"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":2322,"closed_date":1377592297,"accepted_answer_id":2439235,"answer_count":6,"score":4,"last_activity_date":1377525994,"creation_date":1268500677,"last_edit_date":1377525994,"question_id":2439216,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2439216/how-to-teach-beginners-reversing-a-string-in-python","closed_reason":"Opinion-based","title":"How to teach beginners reversing a string in Python?","body":"<p>I am teaching a course \"Introduction to Computer Programming\" to the first year math students. One has to assume that this is the first exposure of students to computer programming. Here are the main goals of my teaching:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>Students should learn and understand the basics of Python.</li>\n<li>Eventually they need to master sufficiently many Python tools so that they are able to select the right tool for a given problem.</li>\n<li>At the same time they have to learn basic skills of problem solving by computer programming.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>My method of teaching is to give for each newly introduced concept a series of problems and teasers that motivate students. For instance, when introducing strings and lists a natural question is the task of string or list reversal. If I ask students to write a code that will check whether a string is a palindrome then I better tell them how to reverse it.</p>\n\n<p>For lists, a natural solution <code>myString.reverse()</code> has at least two drawbacks:</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li>It does not carry over to strings.</li>\n<li>Students will see it a <em>magic</em> unless told about methods first.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p>The real question is: How should one introduce the problem of reversing a string in Python?</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","printing"],"owner":{"account_id":14378682,"reputation":2549,"user_id":10386511,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/cdb7a1378e969d3ebc4e0163ff07411a?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"mangokitty","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/10386511/mangokitty"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":368,"closed_date":1597930489,"accepted_answer_id":57624598,"answer_count":2,"score":-2,"last_activity_date":1597930135,"creation_date":1566556290,"question_id":57624477,"link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/57624477/print-method-invalid-syntax-reversing-a-string","closed_reason":"Not suitable for this site","title":"Print method &quot;invalid syntax&quot; reversing a string","body":"<p>Trying to reverse a string in python and can't figure out what is wrong with my program that this is seen as invalid syntax. </p>\n\n<pre><code>print(r)\n        ^\nSyntaxError: invalid syntax```\n\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>Thanks so much here is my code.</p>\n\n<pre><code>\ns = \"Hello! my name is MangoKitty\"\nr = ''.join(reversed(s.split(''))\nprint(r)\n</code></pre>\n"},{"tags":["python","python-2.7","slice"],"owner":{"account_id":3020211,"reputation":1708,"user_id":2561445,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":39,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/2895eff69ffb6a335ba26e997af637c8?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"bawejakunal","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/2561445/bawejakunal"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":1595,"answer_count":2,"score":3,"last_activity_date":1621442512,"creation_date":1477452766,"question_id":40253256,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/40253256/reverse-string-python-slice-notation","title":"Reverse string Python slice notation","body":"<pre><code>string = \"HELLO\"\nprint string[::-1] #as expected\nprint string[0:6:-1] #empty string why ?\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>I was amazed to see how easy it is to reverse a string in python but then I struck upon this and got lost. Can someone please explain why the second reverse does not works ?</p>\n"},{"tags":["string","common-lisp"],"owner":{"account_id":293187,"reputation":18264,"user_id":596361,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":82,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/b7219254970581e53d3b2b162f7f50f8?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Mirzhan Irkegulov","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/596361/mirzhan-irkegulov"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":2596,"accepted_answer_id":13939328,"answer_count":1,"score":4,"last_activity_date":1355855910,"creation_date":1355855269,"last_edit_date":1495540009,"question_id":13939180,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/13939180/reverse-string-in-common-lisp","title":"Reverse string in Common Lisp","body":"<p><strong>How can i reverse a string in Common Lisp?</strong></p>\n\n<p>I want to transform \"Hello World\" into \"dlroW olleH\". In Python it is done using <a href=\"https://stackoverflow.com/q/931092/596361\">extended slice</a>: <code>\"Hello World\"[::-1]</code>.</p>\n"},{"tags":["python-2.7"],"owner":{"user_type":"does_not_exist","display_name":"user5970003"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":1128,"accepted_answer_id":35584931,"answer_count":3,"score":1,"last_activity_date":1456251697,"creation_date":1456250044,"question_id":35584728,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/35584728/reversing-a-string-in-python-word-by-word","title":"Reversing a string in python (WORD by WORD)","body":"<p>How about reversing a string, not by each character but by word.\nLike for example: \"Python is the best programming language\",  the output should be \"language programming best the is Python\", but the problem is that there shouldn't be any predefined function included.</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","python-3.x"],"owner":{"account_id":4139612,"reputation":673,"user_id":3395330,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":0,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/EIBWg.png?s=256","display_name":"Gopal","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/3395330/gopal"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":3622,"answer_count":3,"score":0,"last_activity_date":1681788284,"creation_date":1492682015,"last_edit_date":1492682494,"question_id":43516110,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/43516110/why-should-we-use-join-function-while-reversing-a-string-in-python","title":"Why should we use join() function while reversing a string in python","body":"<p>what is the purpose of <strong>''.join()</strong>  here <br/></p>\n\n<pre><code>print(''.join(reversed(a)))\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>can't we reverse a string only with reversed function <br/></p>\n\n<pre><code>print(reversed(\"python\"))\n</code></pre>\n"},{"tags":["python","string","function","recursion","reverse"],"owner":{"account_id":3338993,"reputation":1,"user_id":2805672,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/ee208ead2ca2d40c183e885c1626db21?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"user2805672","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/2805672/user2805672"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":6868,"answer_count":8,"score":0,"last_activity_date":1622477793,"creation_date":1379907040,"last_edit_date":1454001257,"question_id":18951389,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/18951389/reversing-a-string-in-python-recursively","title":"Reversing a String in Python Recursively","body":"<p>For a homework assignment I have to create a recursive function that reverses a string. Here's what I have currently. The last three lines of code were made by the instructor and we aren't allowed to change them. When I run the program, nothing is returned. I think the code to reverse the string is correct, but I'm trying to figure out how to print the result.</p>\n\n<pre><code>def reverse(input_string):\n    if len(input_string) == 0:\n         return input_string\n    else:\n         return reverse(input_string[1:]) + input_string[0]\n\nprint \"Please enter the string you want to reverse: \"\ninitial_input = raw_input()\n\nreverse(initial_input)\n</code></pre>\n"},{"tags":["python"],"owner":{"account_id":19086074,"reputation":1,"user_id":13937336,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/204a0061ae44c18153780dfd51638b90?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"john","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/13937336/john"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":174,"answer_count":5,"score":-7,"last_activity_date":1603553636,"creation_date":1603552188,"last_edit_date":1603552404,"question_id":64514844,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/64514844/how-to-reverse-a-string-number-in-python-with-for-loop","title":"how to reverse a string number in python with for loop","body":"<p>I am trying to reverse a string number from right to wrong with odd index I have done from left to right but can you some one help how to do it from right to left</p>\n<pre><code>for i in range(0, len(number), 2):\n    print(number[i])\n</code></pre>\n<p>something like</p>\n<pre><code>for i in range (-len(length), len(length), -2)\n</code></pre>\n<p>let's say a number 1234567\ni want to print 7,5,3,1.</p>\n"},{"tags":["python"],"owner":{"account_id":379964,"reputation":1303,"user_id":733687,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":86,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/0f0ba32c28d31f162bf436331391311a?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"purpleladydragons","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/733687/purpleladydragons"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":172,"accepted_answer_id":10143876,"answer_count":3,"score":1,"last_activity_date":1334331846,"creation_date":1334331215,"question_id":10143848,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/10143848/reversing-a-string-in-python","title":"Reversing a string in python","body":"<p>I want to find a palindrome in a string.</p>\n\n<pre><code>mystring = \"1234321\"\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>Why does </p>\n\n<pre><code>mystring[3:7:-1] \n</code></pre>\n\n<p>not work, but </p>\n\n<pre><code>second = mystring[3:7]\nreversed = second[::-1]\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>this work?</p>\n"},{"tags":["python","string","reverse"],"owner":{"account_id":99714,"reputation":2624,"user_id":269181,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":91,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/968d700efe38dce8e9cce18360980325?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"PeterM","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/users/269181/peterm"},"is_answered":true,"view_count":27202,"accepted_answer_id":5864313,"answer_count":14,"score":43,"last_activity_date":1562520094,"creation_date":1304387333,"last_edit_date":1304401243,"question_id":5864271,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","link":"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/5864271/reverse-a-string-in-python-two-characters-at-a-time-network-byte-order","title":"Reverse a string in Python two characters at a time (Network byte order)","body":"<p>Say you have this string:</p>\n\n<pre><code>ABCDEFGH\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>And you want to reverse it so that it becomes:</p>\n\n<pre><code>GHEFCDAB\n</code></pre>\n\n<p>What would be the most efficient / pythonic solution?  I've tried a few different things but they all look horrible...</p>\n\n<p>Thanks in advance!</p>\n\n<p><strong>Update</strong>:</p>\n\n<p>In case anyone's interested, this wasn't for homework. I had a script that was processing data from a network capture and returning it as a string of hex bytes. The problem was the data was still in network order. Due to the way the app was written, I didn't want to go back through and try to use say socket.htons, I just wanted to reverse the string. </p>\n\n<p>Unfortunately my attempts seemed so hideous, I knew there must be a better way (a more pythonic solution) - hence my question here. </p>\n"}],"has_more":true,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":287}